          "powder_feeding_rate_g_min": "7-9",
          "spot_diameter_mm": 1.8,
          "wavelength_nm": 1070,
          "distance_laser_head_to_melt_pool_mm": 8
        }
      },
      "input_state": "mixed powder",
      "output_state": "as-deposited",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": "2",
          "section": "2.1 Material preparation",
          "quote": "As shown in Fig. 2(a), during the laser melting deposition process, the mixed powders were conveyed to the laser melt pool on a 316L substrate through a coaxial nozzle. The argon gas flow rate was set between 12 and 20 L/min, and the powder feeding rate ranged from 7 to 9 g/min. Argon gas was introduced into the printing chamber to provide protection, and the water and oxygen content inside the chamber was kept below 15 ppm. Wavelength 1070 nm, laser beam distributes like a top hat [47], spot diameter 1.8 mm, laser power 800 W, and scanning speed 400 mm/min were set as the processing parameters for the Ytterbium-doped fiber laser unit. The distance between the laser head and the melting pool is 8 mm, and the laser head is raised by 0.2 mm after each scan.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 2(a)",
          "chunk_id": "e5172ef166d9015e:part:001"
        }
      ]
    },
